From b3cd14afd42aa95f19874e3ae63c5ee95f5a3e01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:00:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] Reconstruct the TCP reassembly helpers and finish the
 options relocation

Recover tcp_reass_create_qent, tcp_reass_destroy_qent, and
tcp_reassq_free from the reference image: the zone allocation and
mem_acct accounting, the atomic queue-length counter, the tcpcb queue
counters, and the m_chain_capacity bookkeeping.  All tcp_reassembly.c
functions are external in the reference DWARF, so drop the remaining
static qualifiers, declare tcp_reass in tcp_var.h, and replace the
public tcp_subr.c wrappers with the reference tcp_reassq_free call in
tcp_close.

The reference's tcp_process_options is the public tcp_dooptions body
relocated to tcp_options.c.  Route the tcp_input.c and tcp_handshake.c
callers to it, drop the static tcp_input.c copy, and make
tcp_finalize_options and tcp_addoptions external like their DWARF
entries.

The TFO helpers are external functions of tcp_fastopen.c in the
reference.  Remove the duplicate static definitions left in
tcp_output.c and tcp_subr.c, drop the unused tcp_subr.c TFO crypto
context, and declare the TFO entry points in tcp_fastopen.h.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
